/* ============================================================================
   complex-fraction-simplify.epher -- 1/(2 + 3i) + 1/(1 - i) as a + bi

   To divide by a complex number, multiply numerator and denominator by the
   conjugate of the denominator: 1/(2 + 3i) = (2 - 3i)/13 and 1/(1 - i) =
   (1 + i)/2 (Churchill and Brown, "Complex Variables and Applications",
   sec. 5). The denominators (2 + 3i)(2 - 3i) = 13 and (1 - i)(1 + i) = 2
   are exact, and the sum is 17/26 + (7/26)i = 0.653846153846 +
   0.269230769231i, displayed to about 12 digits; the last boolean compares
   the sum with the exact fractions.

   Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/algebra/complex/complex-fraction-simplify.epher"

   No knobs to edit; the fractions below are fixed examples.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
z1 = 1 / (2 + 3i)                 // 1/(2 + 3i), echoes (2 - 3i)/13 in decimals
z2 = 1 / (1 - i)                  // 1/(1 - i), echoes 0.5 + 0.5i
z1 + z2                           // the sum, echoes 0.653846153846+0.269230769231i
print("conjugate route for z1:", conj(2 + 3i) / ((2 + 3i) * conj(2 + 3i)))
print("(2 + 3i)(2 - 3i):", (2 + 3i) * conj(2 + 3i))
print("matches 17/26 + 7i/26:", abs(z1 + z2 - (17 / 26 + i * 7 / 26)) < 1e-12)
/* ---- expected output ----
= 0.153846153846-0.230769230769i
= 0.5+0.5i
= 0.653846153846+0.269230769231i
= conjugate route for z1: 0.153846153846-0.230769230769i
= (2 + 3i)(2 - 3i): 13
= matches 17/26 + 7i/26: true
*/
